  "interpretation_notes": [
    "The source's 'voiceless'/'voiced' labels identify orthographic consonant series; they are not claims that all modern consonants in the class are voiceless/voiced.",
    "Some vowel-sign label diacritics are unclear in the scanned table. Preserve the transcription and ambiguity flag; do not infer a Unicode sign mapping from this file alone.",
    "For the ā row in the voiced-series column, the source prints [eə] with parenthetical ([i·ə]); §1.2 says ordinary Phnom Penh speech uses [i·ə] while formal/school pronunciation uses [ee].",
    "The table is a historical descriptive source and dialect discussion, not acoustic gold and not a direct deterministic IPA rule table.",
    "Short i, y and u are described as checked vowels requiring a coda; without a written final consonant, the source describes glottal closure. Several spellings are analyzed as having implicit final /y/ or /w/. See the accompanying audit for page-located details."
